# Notation ratchet (PR #1188, R1188-U6 and R1188-U7;
# docs/links-notation-style.md).
#
# The ceilings on the links notation we own, per scope of
# data/meta/notation-rules.lino, measured by scripts/measure-notation.mjs
# (gate check-notation). Each count is of distinct items, so a new record
# that reuses existing keys moves nothing, while a new `_` name, a new
# abbreviated name, a new duplicated block or a new repeated field raises a
# count and fails the gate. The ceilings only fall: `--write` lowers them to
# the measure after a rule pass. `characters` is recorded for the concise-form
# passes and is not a ceiling, since new seed data rightly adds characters.
#
# History. On 2026-10-08 the seed-lexemes family wrote 4916 lexemes in the
# concise form (`lexeme en "read" "open"` with the fields its surfaces share
# below it): data/seed fell from 3,532,300 to 3,150,411 characters and its
# duplicated blocks from 45 to 27. Its repeated fields were re-based from 115
# to 184 by the same change, not by new repetition: a field every surface of a
# lexeme shares (`part_of_speech noun`) now sits once on the lexeme, where the
# measure sees the same field on the sibling lexemes of other languages. That
# is the next deduplication: state it once on the meaning.
#
# On 2026-10-09 data/seed underscore-names was raised from 9419 to 9426 for
# R1188-U18 ("formalize <url>"): the meaning page_formalization, its role
# page_formalization_action and five answer intents (page_formalization_empty,
# _fetch_failed, _more, _offline, _summary). Intents and roles are identifiers
# both roots and the API read, and their family has not been converted, so a
# member spelled with `-` alone would mix two conventions in one family; it
# converts with its readers in the intents-and-roles pass. The 25 new response
# records of the same change are already written with `-`.
#
# On 2026-11-15 data/meta underscore-names was raised from 2067 to 2069 for
# issue #1550 (PR #1576). The two names are Rust functions that
# data/meta/debug-stage-sources.lino, a table generated from the source tree,
# now lists as the emitters of the validation stage: record_answer_test and
# try_synthesize_from_sub_results, which record the executed test of an answer.
# Rust spells function names with `_`, so the generated table cannot write them
# with `-`; no hand-written record gained a `_` name.
notation-ratchet
  scope data/meta
    underscore-names 2017
    abbreviated-names 198
    duplicated-blocks 9
    repeated-fields 78
    characters 2100270
  scope data/seed
    underscore-names 9265
    abbreviated-names 245
    duplicated-blocks 26
    repeated-fields 183
    characters 3674130
